# Server Information

This document provides details on building, deploying, and testing the Go server component of the `hello` project.

## Implementation

The main server logic is implemented in Go and can be found in [server/cmd/main.go](mdc:server/cmd/main.go). It uses ConnectRPC for handling RPCs.

## RPC Service

The server implements the `GreeterService` defined in the Protobuf schema at [proto/hello/v1/hello.proto](mdc:proto/hello/v1/hello.proto).

- **Service Name:** `hello.v1.GreeterService`
- **Method:** `SayHello`
- **Request Type:** `hello.v1.SayHelloRequest`
- **Response Type:** `hello.v1.SayHelloResponse`

## Building

### Local Build

You can build the server locally using the Go toolchain:

```bash
# Navigate to the server directory
cd server
# Build the binary
go build ./cmd/main.go
```

### Docker Build

A Dockerfile is provided for containerizing the server: [server/Dockerfile](mdc:server/Dockerfile).

```bash
# Navigate to the server directory
cd server
# Build the Docker image
docker build -t hello-server .
```

## Deployment

### Local Deployment

Run the server directly using Go:

```bash
# Navigate to the server directory
cd server
# Run the main application
go run cmd/main.go
```
The server listens on port `8080`.

### Docker Deployment

Run the server using the Docker image:

```bash
docker run -p 8080:8080 hello-server
```

### Docker Compose Deployment

A Docker Compose file is available at [docker-compose.yml](mdc:docker-compose.yml) for easier management.

```bash
docker-compose up -d server
```

## Testing

You can test the running server using `grpcurl` or `curl`. See examples in the [server/README.md](mdc:server/README.md).

### Using `grpcurl`

```bash
grpcurl \
  -plaintext \
  -d '{"name": "World"}' \     
  localhost:8080 \
  hello.v1.GreeterService/SayHello
```

### Using `curl`

```bash
curl \
  --header "Content-Type: application/json" \
  --header "Connect-Protocol-Version: 1" \
  --data '{"name": "World"}' \
  --request POST \
  http://localhost:8080/hello.v1.GreeterService/SayHello
```
